<title>UK: BT seen paying 1.0 bln stg of utility tax.</title>
<headline>BT seen paying 1.0 bln stg of utility tax.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Telecommunications Plc is likely to shoulder around 1.0 billion pounds of a one-off tax on privatised utilities announced by the Labour government, investment analysts said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>But analysts added they believed it unlikely that the telecoms giant would follow through its threats and mount a legal challenge against the proposed tax.  </p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7987</p>
</text>
